Source data
-----------

The data published here originates with New Zealand government agencies and
remains under its publishers' licences, not under MIT. The publishers are:

  - the Ministry of Social Development (including StudyLink)
  - the Ministry of Education (Education Counts)
  - the Treasury

DATA_SOURCES.yaml is the authoritative record. For every dataset it states the
publisher, the source URL, the licence, the basis on which that licence was
established and the URL it was read from, the date the files were retrieved and
exactly how the data was modified. ATTRIBUTION.md carries the same record in
readable form, grouped by publisher.

Licence status: verified 2026-08-30
-----------------------------------

Every one of the 25 sourced datasets was checked against its publisher online on
2026-08-30. All 25 carry a named licence and every one is a clean attribution
licence. None is unverified.

  - CC BY 4.0 International (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
    for 24 datasets — all Ministry of Social Development, Ministry of Education
    (Education Counts) and Treasury material published from 2018 onward.

  - CC BY 3.0 New Zealand (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/nz/)
    for one: the legacy Child, Youth and Family national and local level data of
    June 2017. MSD relicensed from 3.0 NZ to 4.0 International between the 2017
    and 2018 release vintages, and the 2017 files still carry the older mark.
    That function transferred to Oranga Tamariki in April 2017; Oranga Tamariki
    publishes the successor series, also under CC BY 3.0 NZ, and none of its data
    is used here.

Each licence is recorded with a licence_basis:

  - dataset_page (15 datasets) — read from the dataset's own page or its own
    data.govt.nz catalogue record, which carries an explicit licence_id.

  - agency_record (10 datasets) — only an agency-wide or site-wide statement was
    found, not one specific to that dataset. These keep licence_issue: true. The
    licence is very probably right, but it was inherited rather than asserted for
    that dataset in particular. Six are MSD series with no data.govt.nz record;
    four are the Treasury workbooks, whose publication pages return HTTP 403 to
    every scripted request.

None of the three publishers puts a licence statement in the body of its
statistics pages; all three rely on a single site-wide copyright page. The three
statements, and the evidence URL behind every row, are quoted in ATTRIBUTION.md.

Anyone intending to redistribute this data, or to rely on it beyond reading this
demonstration, should confirm the licence on each publisher's own page first —
particularly for the ten agency_record rows.

Modification
------------

The data has been modified. It was downloaded, staged as faithful cell grids,
resolved out of the publishers' worksheet layouts into a conformed mart, and
trimmed to the period range the application charts. Figures are reconciled
against the agencies' published totals, but this is not an official publication
of any agency and no agency has endorsed it. For any official purpose, consult
the agencies directly.

Generated data
--------------

The indicative geography centroids and H3 cells in DIM_GEOGRAPHY are not agency
data. They were authored for this repository because no agency publishes
coordinates alongside these statistics. They are demonstration-only reference
values, offered as CC0: they position a map marker and never change a count.

No synthetic or modelled statistical values exist anywhere in this platform.
